## Decision and status

Proposed replacement for [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).
Keep that accepted record unchanged as history. The desk must not continue merging by
subject alone while a parser fix is queued: a matching symptom can hide a different cause.

The [original incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says “one issue, one fix queued.”
Its computed views contradict that conclusion. The following views use the exported data,
not the age or confidence of the prose. They are not a live connection to the desk.

## What belongs in each ticket

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

- **Parser:** the shared parser reads month first although the tenant writes day first.
  Correct the parsing contract; test app, email and eligible booking-v2 form inputs.
- **Hint:** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` for day-first tenants, but its form reads
  the tenant's way. Correct the displayed hint and form contract independently of the parser.
- The five reports noted as a one-day move remain counted under their computed tenant-based
  cause and are footnoted in the table. Symptom wording alone does not establish a third bug.
  Preserve those observations for follow-up rather than dropping them.

One GitHub issue per cause records its unique report count:
[shared parser](https://github.com/madpawel/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) and
[booking-v3 hint](https://github.com/madpawel/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
No production fix was performed by this harness.

## Engineering outcome — desk update

The [course's engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows)
now reports that #4471 closed on 5 October:

- **Parser: fixed.** Engineering's change is `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
  The [parser issue](https://github.com/madpawel/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)
  is closed as completed.
- **Hint: won't fix.** The booking-v3 form was retired, rather than its hint being fixed.
  The [hint issue](https://github.com/madpawel/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)
  is closed as not planned. Retirement is not a shipped correction to the old form.

This update was read on 29 October 2026. It is newer than the 4 October data export;
the views below remain historical report counts, not a live unresolved queue.
The proposed triage-rule replacement is separate from these engineering outcomes.

## Counting and attribution

Deduplicate overlapping export pages by report ID, then select reports merged into this ticket.
Use the tenant directory's locale and booking form with the report's channel.
Do not classify by browser locale, subject, or intake tag: the tagged-as column
shows the intake guesses disagree with the cause.

The source of truth for these calculations is `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, together with
`locales.ts`, tenant JSON and `reports-4471.json`. Counts are computed at render time;
a future export can change them without rewriting a paragraph.

## When the problem arrived, and when the desk merged it

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Read the received and merged bars separately. The large early-July merge bar records
backlog consolidation, not a sudden onset of the incident. Reports arrived earlier and
continue afterwards. Fixing how the desk labels a ticket does not stop new reports.

The chart uses Monday–Sunday weeks and the source date portion of each timestamp,
as implemented in `QueueTimeline.svelte`; it does not convert those dates to UTC.

## Replacement triage procedure

1. Collapse repeated report IDs. Preserve the original body and time fields.
2. Resolve the tenant from the directory. Check its actual locale and booking form.
3. Compare causes using the channel and tenant configuration, not the subject.
4. Same known cause: merge into that cause's ticket. Different causes: keep separate.
5. Unknown tenant or unplaced cause: investigate; never merge simply because subjects match.
6. Recompute counts and re-read the evidence when the desk or tenant configuration changes.
   Keep this export's scope distinct from a claim about the live queue.

<DedupeExplorer />

App and email can be the same cause despite different subjects.
The same subject at one tenant can be different causes across app and form.
Different tenants can also use different forms. The examples above execute these checks.

## Consequences

Engineering gets independent fixes with auditable report counts.
The desk must read enough context to identify a cause, rather than saving time by
silently mixing unrelated reports. Keep accepted decision history intact; update the
triage instructions only after this replacement is adopted and reviewed.

